      "message": "feat(simview): camcraft-sim check judges a 3-axis G-code file headless\n\nAdd the crate crates/simview (package camcraft-simview) with the binary\ncamcraft-sim. It has no edge to camcraft-app or camcraft-ui.\n\n- `camcraft-sim cl <file.cl> ...` is the old sim-crate binary, moved\n  with the same arguments, output and exit codes.\n- `camcraft-sim check <file.nc> --stock <box> --tools <T map>\n  (--post <.cps> | --dialect <name>) [--machine <.mch>] [--wcs G54=x,y,z]\n  [--fixture <box>] [--cell <mm>]` parses the program with\n  camcraft-gcode and runs:\n  - the post manifest checks (kind served, programUnits, workOffsetMax);\n  - the stock check (a rapid through the material that is left);\n  - the holder law (shank and holder bands against that material);\n  - the fixture law (verify's region-free laws over --fixture boxes);\n  - the machine limits (#2585, in program coordinates);\n  - the machine-part collision on the generated model (#2584).\n- Exit 0: each check ran and passed. 1: bad input. 2: a check failed,\n  with its NC line. 3: a check was not judged, named.\n- A/B/C words refuse by name (the gcode parser). An unmapped T and a\n  .camtools library refuse by name (#4465 follows up the library).\n\nThe decision files carry the #2574 research decisions with the crate\nedges, and the unattended decisions of this slice.\n\nFixes #2586\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
